<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41833" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπόπτ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπόψομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>overseer, watcher,</i> esp. of a
			god, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πυθῶνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					9.5
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				266
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ πάντων ἐ. θεός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Es.</u>
					5.1
				</span></i>
			 ; title of Poseidon, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				8.30.1
			</span></i> ; of the Sun, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				666.25
			</span></i> (Egypt, <span class="entity">i A. D.</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαίμονες ἐ. τῶν ἀνθρωπίνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ti.Locr.
					105a
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥσπερ ἐπόπτας τῶν στρατηγουμένων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					4.25
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. γῆς καὶ θαλάσσης,</span> of
			Pompey, <i><span class="en">
				<u>JHS</u>
				27.64
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Cyzicus</span>); of Augustus, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IGRom.</u>
				4.309
			</span></i> (Pergam.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. εἰρήνης,</span> of
			a police <i>magistrate,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				POxy.
				991
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> simply, <i>spectator,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					301
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>inspector,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Cod.Just.
				10.16.13
			</span></i>
			<u>Intr.</u>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>one admitted to the highest grade of the mysteries,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				12.6.51
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				22
			</span></i>, etc., cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφόπται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12(8).205.3
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Samothrace</span>) : c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυστηρίων ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Michel</u>
					1141
				</span></i>
			 (ibid.) ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινος</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>PMag.Lond.</u>
				121.572
			</span></i> : metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τῆς ἐκείνου μεγαλειότητος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>2 Ep.Pet.</u>
					1.16
				</span></i>
			.</div>
